Guided Exercise: Inspect Kubernetes Resources (Explained)
1️⃣ Start the Lab Environment
lab start cli-resources
What it does
•	Prepares the OpenShift cluster for the exercise
•	Creates a project (namespace) called cli-resources
•	Deploys an example application myapp
________________________________________
2️⃣ Login to the Cluster
oc login -u developer -p developer https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
Explanation
•	oc = OpenShift CLI
•	login authenticates you to the cluster
•	developer = normal application user
________________________________________
3️⃣ Select the Project
oc project cli-resources
Explanation
OpenShift uses projects (namespaces) to isolate resources.
Example resources inside a project:
•	pods
•	deployments
•	services
•	configmaps
________________________________________
4️⃣ List All Supported Kubernetes Resource Types
oc api-resources
This command shows:
Column	Meaning
NAME	Resource name
SHORTNAME	CLI shortcut
APIVERSION	API group + version
NAMESPACED	Whether resource belongs to namespace
KIND	Object type
Example:
NAME	SHORTNAME	APIVERSION	NAMESPACED	KIND
pods	po	v1	true	Pod
nodes	no	v1	false	Node
deployments	deploy	apps/v1	true	Deployment
________________________________________
5️⃣ Show Only Namespaced Resources
oc api-resources --namespaced
Why?
These resources exist inside projects.
Examples:
•	Pods
•	Deployments
•	Services
•	ConfigMaps
________________________________________
Count them
oc api-resources --namespaced -o name | wc -l
Example result:
122
Meaning:
Cluster supports 122 namespaced resource types
________________________________________
6️⃣ Show Non-Namespaced Resources
oc api-resources --namespaced=false
Examples:
•	nodes
•	namespaces
•	clusteroperators
•	persistentvolumes
________________________________________
Count them
oc api-resources --namespaced=false -o name | wc -l
Example:
129
Meaning:
Cluster has 129 cluster-wide resource types
________________________________________
7️⃣ Show Resources From Core API Group
oc api-resources --api-group ''
Core API group contains
Basic Kubernetes resources like:
•	Pods
•	Services
•	Nodes
•	ConfigMaps
•	Secrets
Example output:
NAME	KIND
pods	Pod
services	Service
nodes	Node
configmaps	ConfigMap
________________________________________
8️⃣ Understand a Resource Schema
Example: Pods
oc explain pods
Shows
•	Description
•	Fields
•	Structure
Example fields:
apiVersion
kind
metadata
spec
status
________________________________________
9️⃣ List Pods in the Project
oc get pods
Example:
NAME                     READY   STATUS
myapp-54fcdcd9d7-2h5vx   1/1     Running
Meaning:
•	Pod belongs to deployment myapp
________________________________________
🔟 Inspect Pod Details
oc describe pod myapp-54fcdcd9d7-2h5vx
Shows
•	Container image
•	IP address
•	Events
•	Restart count
•	Scheduler info
Example:
Image: registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/ubi8/httpd-24
IP: 10.8.0.127
________________________________________
11️⃣ View Pod as YAML
oc get pod myapp-54fcdcd9d7-2h5vx -o yaml
YAML shows full object structure
Example:
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: myapp-54fcdcd9d7
spec:
  containers:
  - name: myapp
    image: ubi8/httpd-24
Difference
Command	Use
describe	human readable
get -o yaml/json	machine structured
________________________________________
12️⃣ Resources From Apps API Group
oc api-resources --api-group apps
Example resources:
Resource	Purpose
deployments	manage pods
replicasets	maintain pod replicas
daemonsets	run pod on every node
statefulsets	stateful applications
________________________________________
13️⃣ Understand Deployment Schema
oc explain deployments
Deployment manages:
•	Pod replicas
•	Rolling updates
•	Scaling
________________________________________
14️⃣ List Deployments
oc get deploy
Example:
NAME   READY
myapp  1/1
________________________________________
15️⃣ Show Deployment Details
oc get deploy myapp -o wide
Shows:
CONTAINERS: myapp
IMAGE: registry.ocp4.example.com/ubi8/httpd
________________________________________
16️⃣ Describe Deployment
oc describe deployment myapp
Shows:
•	replicas
•	update strategy
•	events
•	ReplicaSet
Example:
Replicas: 1 desired | 1 available
Strategy: RollingUpdate
________________________________________
17️⃣ OpenShift Configuration API Group
oc api-resources --api-group config.openshift.io
These resources configure the cluster itself.
Examples:
Resource	Purpose
clusteroperators	cluster components
clusterversion	cluster version
infrastructure	platform details
networks	networking
scheduler	pod scheduling
________________________________________
18️⃣ Project Resource
oc explain projects
Project
OpenShift equivalent of namespace.
Contains:
•	users
•	quotas
•	resources
________________________________________
19️⃣ Describe Project
oc describe project cli-resources
Shows:
•	labels
•	annotations
•	quotas
•	status
Example:
Status: Active
________________________________________
20️⃣ Get Project as JSON
oc get project cli-resources -o json
Shows structured output:
apiVersion: project.openshift.io/v1
kind: Project
metadata:
  name: cli-resources
________________________________________
21️⃣ Cluster Services Access
Developer user cannot access system namespaces.
Example:
oc get pods -n openshift-etcd
Error:
Forbidden
Because:
developer ≠ cluster admin
________________________________________
22️⃣ Login as Admin
oc login -u admin -p redhatocp
________________________________________
23️⃣ List ETCD Pods
oc get pods -n openshift-etcd
Example:
etcd-master01
ETCD stores:
•	cluster state
•	configuration
•	metadata
________________________________________
24️⃣ Extract Container Image Using JSONPath
oc get pods etcd-master01 -n openshift-etcd \
-o=jsonpath='{.spec.containers[0].image}'
Example output:
quay.io/openshift-release-dev/ocp-v4
________________________________________
25️⃣ Same Using jq
oc get pod etcd-master01 -o json | jq .spec.containers[0].image
________________________________________
26️⃣ Same Using Go Template
oc get pod etcd-master01 \
-o go-template='{{(index .spec.containers 0).image}}'
________________________________________
27️⃣ Filter YAML with yq
oc get pod prometheus-k8s-0 -n openshift-monitoring -o yaml | yq '.status.conditions'
Shows pod conditions:
Ready
Initialized
ContainersReady
PodScheduled
________________________________________
28️⃣ Custom Columns Output
Example:
oc get pods -n openshift-storage \
-o custom-columns=PodName:".metadata.name",\
ContainerName:"spec.containers[].name",\
Phase:"status.phase",\
IP:"status.podIP",\
Ports:"spec.containers[].ports[].containerPort"
Output:
PodName        ContainerName  Phase   IP        Ports
lvms-operator  manager        Running 10.8.0.97 9443
________________________________________
29️⃣ Finish Lab
lab finish cli-resources
Why?
•	Clean environment
•	Avoid conflicts with next labs
